@startuml login
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam shadowing false
title Login: Offer Publication, Import and Independent Sign-Out (current serial flow)

actor "User" as User
participant "SyncService" as Service
participant "LoginSync" as Login
participant "SyncRepository" as Repo
participant "AccountStore" as Account
participant "Temporary MusicClient" as Candidate
participant "Local MusicClient" as Client

== Refresh and publish offers ==
opt login domain refresh requested
  Service -> Login : read
  Login -> Repo : readLoginKey
  Repo --> Login : login-key.json (or none)
  Login -> Login : when the key description changes, load the key from the local Keychain\ntreat a verifier mismatch as locked
  Login -> Repo : read(.login)
  Repo --> Login : valid device records / conflict versions\nsingle-device read errors logged and isolated
  Login -> Login : cache records, observe counters\nupdate withdrawal duty when this device's record is read
end
Service -> Login : publish(enabled: loginEnabled at this moment)
Login -> Account : check profile / authenticatedAccountID / hasAuthCookie
alt sharing allowed, unlocked and account authenticated
  Login -> Client : read authentication cookies
  Login -> Login : unchanged content keeps the previous offer\notherwise seal cookies with AES-GCM → outgoingLogin
else sharing off, locked, or no local cookie
  Login -> Login : outgoingLogin = nil
else cookie present but account not yet verified
  Login --> Service : keep the existing offer; return other devices' accounts
end
opt outgoingLogin decided and content changed, or withdrawal still owed
  Login -> Repo : write this device's login.json (payload or tombstone)
  Repo --> Login : success
  Login -> Login : update local cache and hasPublishedLogin
end
Login --> Service : latest valid offers from other devices (current key only) → logins

== Set or enter the sync passphrase ==
alt folder has no key, or the user resets it
  User -> Service : createLoginKey(passphrase, confirmation)
  Service -> Login : createKey
  Login -> Login : PBKDF2 in the background; new salt and key ID
  Login -> Repo : writeLoginKey
else folder already has a key
  User -> Service : unlockLogin(passphrase)
  Service -> Login : unlock
  Login -> Login : PBKDF2 in the background; compare verifier
end
Login -> Login : save the key to the local Keychain
Service -> Service : await synchronizeNow (login)

== User confirms import ==
User -> Service : importLogin(record)
Service -> Service : no concurrent imports; capture connection generation\nre-check the offer is still listed on this connection
Service -> Login : open(login)
Login --> Service : decrypted cookies (asks for the passphrase when locked)
Service -> Account : importLogin(accountID, cookies, authorization)
Account -> Account : check payload and current authorization\nrecord bootstrapGeneration / authenticationFingerprint
Account -> Candidate : set candidate cookies; query the account online
Candidate --> Account : verified profile
Account -> Account : re-check account ID, authorization,\nbootstrap generation and original fingerprint
Account -> Client : replaceAuthentication (applied after persisting)
Account -> Account : bump authentication generation; suspend old playback\napply profile and local account snapshot
Account --> Service : local credential import complete
Service -> Service : re-check cancellation / connection / current account\nset loginEnabled = true and save
Service -> Service : await synchronizeNow\nrefreshing: login / publishing: login + playback
Service -> Account : await refreshLibrary()
Account --> Service : library refresh finished
Service --> User : whether the current account still matches\ndefer clears importingLogin
note over Service,Account
  The interaction still waits for the follow-up sync and library refresh;
  it does not return as soon as the credentials are committed.
  Cancellation or connection changes after the commit do not undo the imported credentials.
end note

== Local sign-out ==
User -> Account : logout()
Account -> Service : shouldRevokeLoginSession(current account ID)
Service -> Login : isAccountSharedElsewhere(account ID, this device's ID)
Login --> Service : whether another device's latest record still offers the account
Service --> Account : revoke by default; keep only when sync and login sync are on\nand the account is offered elsewhere
Account -> Client : clearAuthCookies (local)
Account -> Account : bump bootstrap generation, clear local snapshot, apply signed-out state
Account -> Service : profile change → merged login / playback publication request
opt server session must be revoked
  Account -> Candidate : request /logout with the cookies from before sign-out
  Candidate --> Account : success or thrown error; never touches a newer local login
end
Service -> Login : publish → withdraw this device's offer
note over Repo,Client
  Cookies in the sync folder are sealed with a key derived from the sync passphrase;
  the key lives only in each device's Keychain.
  The server session is revoked by default and kept only while another device
  still offers the account; the last device out revokes it.
  With sync off, nothing is withdrawn from the cloud until it reconnects.
end note
@enduml
